 Passwords, confirmation links, cookies, databases and local email files are not included in the repository or download. There are no default credentials.
 
+### Working test account
+
+Stop the app, then run:
+
+```sh
+dotnet run --project src/SrSimplifyRoutine.Web --launch-profile http -- --create-demo
+dotnet run --project src/SrSimplifyRoutine.Web --launch-profile http
+```
+
+The first command creates a new, confirmed local test account and prints its unique email and random password. Copy them into the login form. It exits after creating the account; the second command starts the app at http://localhost:5127. Existing accounts are not modified. This command is refused in Production. Never share a development database with production.
+
+### Send real email
+
+Without SMTP configuration, local development intentionally delivers only to the local inbox. To receive real messages, configure your provider's SMTP host, verified sender, username and password using **user secrets** (the project has a UserSecretsId) or environment variables. Do not commit credentials. STARTTLS is required; use the provider's STARTTLS port (usually 587, not implicit TLS port 465).
+
+After supplying the settings listed below, verify SMTP independently:
+
+```sh
+dotnet run --project src/SrSimplifyRoutine.Web --launch-profile http -- --test-email your-address@example.com
+```
+
+A nonzero exit indicates a configuration or delivery error. SMTP acceptance does not guarantee inbox placement: also check spam, the provider's delivery logs and sender/domain verification. Then use **Resend confirmation** for an already-created account. Anonymous responses intentionally do not disclose whether an email is registered. Old confirmation/reset links expire after two hours.
+
 ## Features
 
 - Registration, confirmed-email login, logout, temporary lockout and password recovery.
